              <field>
                <name>BUSTURN</name>
                <description>Bus turnaround phase duration
These bits are written by software to add a delay at the end of current write transaction to next transaction on the same bank.
For FRAM memories, the bus turnaround delay should be configured to match the minimum t&lt;sub&gt;PC&lt;/sub&gt; (precharge time) timings. The bus turnaround delay is inserted between any consecutive transactions on the same bank (read/read, write/write, read/write and write/read). The chip select is toggling between any consecutive accesses.
(BUSTURN + 1)HCLK period ≥ tPC min
...</description>
